# Fixtures that are compared BYTE-FOR-BYTE against something produced in
# memory must never have their line endings translated on checkout.
#
# Without this, every golden test fails on a Windows runner and the diff is
# baffling: the render says "…╮" and the golden says "…╮\r", identical to the
# eye, differing by a carriage return that git inserted at checkout because
# core.autocrlf defaults to true there. Nothing about the product is wrong —
# the measuring instrument was modified on its way out of the repository.
internal/tui/testdata/golden/** -text
internal/sim/testdata/v1/**     -text

# Shell scripts run on Linux hosts and inside Linux containers, including
# scripts/deploy/remote-deploy.sh, which is shipped to the production host and
# executed there. A CRLF shebang line fails with "bad interpreter: no such
# file or directory", which is one of the least informative errors in Unix and
# a spectacularly bad one to meet during a deploy.
*.sh text eol=lf
